    "tags": "pricing, packages, services",
    "summary": "Bailey Ventures Digital helps local service businesses achieve three outcomes:",
    "content": "## Positioning\n\nBailey Ventures Digital helps local service businesses achieve three outcomes:\n\n1. **Get found:** Local SEO and Google Business Profile improvements.\n2. **Convert interest:** Clear, conversion-focused websites and landing experiences.\n3. **Respond and book:** CRM and AI-assisted lead capture, follow-up, and appointment workflows.\n\n## Current package anchors\n\n> Confirm the final scope, setup charges, software/usage fees, term, and support allowance before using these prices in a proposal.\n\n### Growth Essentials — $397/month\n\nBest for a business that needs a clean local visibility and lead-handling foundation with controlled monthly support.\n\n**Approved deliverables:** [[INSERT FINAL DELIVERABLES]]  \n**Setup fee:** [[AMOUNT OR NONE]]  \n**Usage/third-party fees:** [[DETAILS]]  \n**Support allowance:** [[DETAILS]]\n\n### Starter — $697/month\n\nBest for a business ready for consistent implementation across a focused visibility or lead-conversion priority.\n\n**Approved deliverables:** [[INSERT FINAL DELIVERABLES]]  \n**Setup fee:** [[AMOUNT OR NONE]]  \n**Usage/third-party fees:** [[DETAILS]]  \n**Support allowance:** [[DETAILS]]\n\n### Professional — $997/month\n\nThe primary recommended plan for businesses needing a more complete growth system, stronger fulfillment cadence, and deeper reporting.\n\n**Approved deliverables:** [[INSERT FINAL DELIVERABLES]]  \n**Setup fee:** [[AMOUNT OR NONE]]  \n**Usage/third-party fees:** [[DETAILS]]  \n**Support allowance:** [[DETAILS]]\n\n### Scale — $1,497/month\n\nBest for multi-location, higher-volume, or operationally complex businesses requiring broader implementation and priority capacity.\n\n**Approved deliverables:** [[INSERT FINAL DELIVERABLES]]  \n**Setup fee:** [[AMOUNT OR NONE]]  \n**Usage/third-party fees:** [[DETAILS]]  \n**Support allowance:** [[DETAILS]]\n\n## Standalone and project work\n\nWebsite projects, audits, migrations, complex integrations, custom development, content production, ad spend, call/text usage, software subscriptions, and work outside the package must be priced and approved separately unless explicitly included.\n\n## Pricing rules\n\n- Sell the business outcome, then document exact deliverables.\n- Never promise a package before confirming fit and delivery capacity.\n- Reduce scope or phase the project instead of discounting identical work.\n- Identify third-party and usage charges separately.\n- Do not guarantee rankings, leads, bookings, revenue, or platform approvals.\n- The signed agreement and approved scope control over this internal summary."
